module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.binder_renaming_changes_variant_field_lookup

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data binder_renaming_changes_variant_field_lookup: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "binder_renaming_changes_variant_field_lookup" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "**renaming a pattern binder changes which variant field the compiler looks up** (the authored pattern keeps Present { value: ... }, but changing only the bound name changes acceptance and the refusal names the binder as though it were the field. The field label and binder declaration are different facts; alpha-renaming the latter must not rename the former. " ,
    "MEASURED 2026-09-06 while repairing gunbc#10625. One native claim_batch artifact, SHA-256 b9a1ef3faedc231d876ef9d90be61ffeb7f96319d5912d54ed1e8a1228671354, executed a four-cell probe in BuildBuddy invocation f307e235-4aaf-4590-b82a-af6aa9cd2207 (https://app.buildbuddy.io/invocation/f307e235-4aaf-4590-b82a-af6aa9cd2207). The selected helper was v1.tests.claim.algebra_application_refusal_test.structural_receiver_without_application_refuses_at_requested_position; the source variant was in v1.compiler.infer_lookup.lookup_structural_method, selecting a profile from v1.compiler.infer_types.kernel_profile_lookup. " ,
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, all four cells and the same binary: local-bound lookup with Present { value: p } executed PASS; direct lookup expression with that p binder executed PASS; local-bound lookup with Present { value: profile } refused; direct lookup expression with that profile binder refused. Both refusals were field profile not found in type Present. Expression shape is exonerated by this experiment; the refusal follows the binder spelling. This is not the query-grain regression where unrelated ReceiverElement demands poisoned reverse: that repair was already present in the tested binary and its positive/refusal controls passed. " ,
    "TRACED BOUNDARIES, NOT AN INVENTED ROOT CAUSE: v1.compiler.parse.parse_variant_bindings_brace_acc carries field_name separately from the nested Bind declaration into v1.std.core.make_field_binding_node. v1.compiler.infer.extend_scope_with_pattern_node asks v1.std.core.field_binding_name_at, which delegates to authored_name_at and its ident_span source slice, before v1.compiler.infer_patterns.lookup_field_in_variant emits the refusal. The missing relation between these boundaries remains to be traced; this receipt does not claim the parser, source-index construction or projection has been individually convicted. " ,
    "The raw self-compile diagnostic printed dag/std/algebra.dag:8040-8044. Those are byte offsets covering the type token of AlgebraProfile at line 258, not line numbers. lookup_field_in_variant uses the synthesized variant declaration span; the claim_batch renderer reports the same refusal at 258:1. The span does not identify the offending binder use. " ,
    "DISPOSITION: the existing p spelling was retained in the repair as a disclosed workaround, not as a repair of binder-name invariance. No compiler fix or required executing consumer is claimed by filing this row. The four-cell transport was branch-local; the recorded native discrimination does not establish required-floor coverage. " ,
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, as a capability: a required executing consumer checks alpha-renaming of a pattern binder while holding its variant and field identity fixed, and rejects any acceptance or field-identity change. The structural terminal is a field selection carried independently of the binder declaration through every transformation and consumed as that field identity, so substituting the bound name as a field key has no construction path. Filing this receipt establishes neither rung.)" ,
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
